This is because the language injects semicolons automatically to separate statements. This is a gotcha with the language. Your return statement gets converted to this:
   return;
   {
     key : value,
   }

To avoid this problem, you should adopt the practice of putting semicolons in the same line, like this:
    return {
      key : value
    };

Also, do yourself a favor and grab a copy of the Douglas Crockford : The Good Parts. This is clearly mentioned in the book.

